# react-tooltip-native — Cursor rules

- **TypeScript**: Strict mode. No implicit any; prefer explicit types for public API. See docs/API_SPECS.md for the authoritative public API.
- **No runtime dependencies**: Dev dependencies only unless explicitly required.
- **Layout**: All library code under src/. Modules: src/core/, src/strategy/, src/positioning/, src/hooks/, src/components/. See docs/DEV-ARCHITECTURE.md for exact structure.
- **SSR-safe**: Never access window, document, or navigator at module top-level; check at call time inside functions.
- **Native path**: No portals in native path. Top Layer handles rendering. Use Popover API and CSS Anchor Positioning when supported.
- **Fallback path**: No Floating UI. No heavy collision engine. Fallback must use ResizeObserver (trigger + overlay) and scroll listeners on nearest scroll parents only. No global window scroll only, no polling loops, no continuous rAF loops.
- **Behavior parity**: Fallback must match native for auto light-dismiss, manual persistence, Esc, and openChange reason values.
- **Flicker mitigation**: On native show, inject anchor + placement styles then rAF then showPopover() (or visibility gating). No visible (0,0) flash.
- **Bundle**: Keep bundle ≤ 4KB gzip. No external positioning libs, no animation lib, no polyfills bundled. Run npm run size after build.
- **MVP scope**: No feature drift beyond MVP. Non-goals: focus trap, Shadow DOM, follow-cursor, animation framework, full dropdown/menu semantics. See docs/PRD.md.
- **Tests**: Write tests for each module. Vitest (jsdom) for unit; Playwright for E2E using demo app. Do not rely on clipboard or OS-specific APIs in E2E assertions.
- **Definition of done**: Run npm run test:all before marking work done (typecheck, unit, build, size, test:pw).
- **Stepwise workflow**: Change one area at a time (e.g. one module or one doc). Stop for commit before moving to the next area. Do not batch unrelated changes.
- **Single source of truth**: docs/DEV-ARCHITECTURE.md for repo layout and implementation order. docs/PRD.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/API_SPECS.md for product and API.
- **Packaging**: ESM + CJS via tsup; exports map with types, import, require. Publish dist only.
